  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Caritas Brazil emergency appeal for flood funds - 2009</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Weeks of heavy rain in the N&amp;NE of Brazil caused heavy flooding which left an estimated 40 people dead and hundreds of thousands homeless or displaced.  260 Municipalities in the Maranhao and Piaui states (both among the poorest in Brazil) are on emergency alert. Caritas Brasil has launched an appeal with Caritas Internationalis members for funding which will allow regional and diocesan Caritas organisations to get vital supplies to those most in need and especially to those who are in areas which have been cut off from the main transport routes because the roads are impassable.  CAFOD will support Caritas to increase their capacity to carry out the work of collection and distribution of emergency supplies to 5000 affected families.</narrative>
  </description>
